It should not wrap a value in a quote that appears inside a twig drop
singleQuote: true
<div class="{{ foo('a') }}"></div>

It should use the opposite quote when the preferred one appears inside a twig drop
<div class="{{ foo("a") }}"></div>

It should use the opposite quote when the preferred one appears inside a twig tag
singleQuote: true
<div class="{% if a %}{{ b }}{% else %}{{ c('d') }}{% endif %}"></div>

It should keep the original double quotes when the value contains both quote characters
singleQuote: true
<div class="{{ foo('a', "b") }}"></div>

It should keep the original single quotes when the value contains both quote characters
<div class='{{ foo('a', "b") }}'></div>

It should use the preferred quote for unquoted values that contain both quote characters
<div id={{ foo('a', "b") }}></div>

It should not introduce a conflicting quote inside verbatim blocks
singleQuote: true
{% verbatim %}<div class="{{ foo('a') }}"></div>{% endverbatim %}

It should still use the opposite quote when text-like values contain the preferred quote
singleQuote: true
<div data-x="it's"></div>

It should still use the opposite quote when text-like values contain the preferred quote (2)
<div data-x='say "hi"'></div>
